+Only that driver allocates and supplies a dedicated notification channel.
+The reader publishes one success token after dropping its framer and sender;
+queued lines or errors remain untouched. A disconnected notification channel
+without that token is failure, including reader panic. The token proves
+sender drop, not a joined reader thread, clean EOF, child exit or reaping.
+Read errors retain their original queue item, so the unchanged final drain
